domain LatestContract:
  description "Latest output contract execution before normal completion acceptance."
evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  "Owner explicitly selects latest prompt output instructions for existing battle continuations and requires ADR0053 freezing only after normal completion test succeeds."
evidence CURRENT:
  "ADR0053 and ADR0055 preserve old rendering; actual narration builders and frozen source system include legacy single-object grammar."
premise PROTECTED:
  "Retain strict current schemas, committed speech, observer knowledge, bound character/style assets, canonical battle semantics, actual usage and historical records."
premise DESIGN:
  "Supersede ADR0053 and ADR0055 with conditional freezing. Latest templates execute for new and existing continuations before normal completion acceptance; historical stored prompt identity remains history rather than execution authority. Replace conflicting active contract instructions, rebuild dispatch proofs from actual prepared requests, and test prompts generated by implementation including old frozen inputs."
premise UNKNOWN:
  "Historical frozen prose reconstruction must preserve style and observer boundaries; public deployment and normal completion remain unverified."
premise ALTERNATIVES:
  "Keeping old execution contradicts owner choice. Appending current instructions to old grammar retains contradiction. Rewriting all battle engine versions exceeds prompt-only scope."
decision ACCEPTANCE based_on OWNER_ACCEPTANCE, CURRENT, PROTECTED, DESIGN, UNKNOWN, ALTERNATIVES:
  "Record successor ADR before dependent changes. Implement latest-only output instructions without broad engine migration; test real builders and historical continuations, then release through scoped official deployment and verify a new public battle completion. Freezing resumes only after completion evidence is recorded."
